typhoon patch on felucca-bsp: fm1_radio_power, the radio's supplies as V15 leaves them (chip/fm1_sys.h)
SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 (a change to felucca-bsp's MPL-2.0 file)

What: fm1_radio_power(): the four P33 registers M-VAVE's V15 (JieLi's power_init) sets and a Felucca-family firmware
does not: the BT DC-DC configured (P3_ANA_CON7 0xA5, P3_ANA_CON8 0x96), the 1.3 V supply moved from its LDO to the
DC-DC (P3_ANA_CON0: RC 250k, DCDC13 on, then LDO13 off), the radio's 1.2 V LDO automatic (P3_WLDO12_AUTO 0xC0).
Why: after a power-on, without them, the radio's calibration draws more than the LDO gives: the supply sags, flash and
bus reads go wrong, and Bluetooth's start crashes or hangs in the trim (every start after a power cycle, never after
V15 has run; they survive a warm reset). Found in typhoon on its old platform 2026-10-16 by reading every P33 register
after V15 and after a power-on and diffing (typhoon notes/01-bluetooth-start-power.md); there since build 37
(Bluetooth on 5 power cycles in a row). Seen again on fm1-base 2026-10-24 (crashes on switching Bluetooth after a
power cycle): fm1-base's rail raise (fm1_vdc14_raise, fm1_sysvdd_raise) is not enough on this unit.
Applies to: felucca-bsp 4bd6d0b (as fm1-base ced9443 pins it in base/bsp).
Upstream: not offered yet (hugelton/felucca-bsp).

diff --git a/chip/fm1_sys.h b/chip/fm1_sys.h
index 62fa96a..6158eba 100644
--- a/chip/fm1_sys.h
+++ b/chip/fm1_sys.h
@@ -100,6 +100,34 @@ static void fm1_vdc14_raise(uint32_t level)
         fm1_delay_us(100);
     }
 }
+/* The radio's supplies as M-VAVE's own firmware (V15, JieLi's power_init) leaves them. After a power-on the 1.3 V
+ * supply runs from its LDO and the radio's DC-DC is unconfigured; the radio's calibration then draws more than that
+ * gives, the supply sags, and flash and bus reads go wrong: Bluetooth's start crashes or hangs in the trim, on every
+ * start after a power cycle, never after V15 has run (typhoon 2026-10-16: every P33 register read after V15 and
+ * after a power-on, and diffed; notes/01-bluetooth-start-power.md there).
+ *   P3_ANA_CON7     0x00 -> 0xA5  the BT DC-DC: bias, duty, oscillator
+ *   P3_ANA_CON8     0x00 -> 0x96  its V2I resistor, current sense, comparator, zero, ramp
+ *   P3_ANA_CON0     0x77 -> 0xFB  RC 250k on, DCDC13 on, then LDO13 off (the DC-DC first: the rail never drops)
+ *   P3_WLDO12_AUTO  0x00 -> 0xC0  the radio's 1.2 V LDO, automatic
+ * Once at boot, the radio off. They survive a warm reset (an update's restart, the watchdog), not a power-off. The
+ * waits feed no watchdog (its feed is a P33 access too). */
+#define FM1_P3_ANA_CON0 0x00u
+#define FM1_P3_ANA_CON7 0x07u
+#define FM1_P3_ANA_CON8 0x08u
+#define FM1_P3_WLDO12_AUTO 0x74u
+static __attribute__((unused)) void fm1_radio_power(void)
+{
+    fm1_p33_write(FM1_P3_ANA_CON7, 0xA5);
+    fm1_p33_write(FM1_P3_ANA_CON8, 0x96);
+    fm1_p33_or(FM1_P3_ANA_CON0, 0x80);             /* RC_250k_EN */
+    fm1_delay_us(200);
+    fm1_p33_or(FM1_P3_ANA_CON0, 0x08);             /* DCDC13_EN */
+    fm1_delay_us(2000);
+    fm1_p33_and(FM1_P3_ANA_CON0, (uint8_t)~0x04u); /* LDO13_EN off */
+    fm1_delay_us(1000);
+    fm1_p33_write(FM1_P3_WLDO12_AUTO, 0xC0);
+    fm1_delay_us(1000);
+}
 static uint32_t fm1_sysvdd(void) { return fm1_p33_read(FM1_P3_ANA_CON9) & 15u; }
 static void fm1_sysvdd_raise(uint32_t level)
 {
